  "review_notes": [
    "The margin's alternative rendering (over his chariots, and over his horses) was read and set aside; the printed text governs (rule 38).",
    "them at t024 is added under rule 44: the coordinated clause gaps its object and writes no object morpheme, so no morpheme in it answers to the pronoun. This agrees with 1SA.8.12, 1SA.8.14 and 1SA.8.16, which mark the same supplied pronoun added. The competing reading, taken by the original pass, gave it to בְּנֵי as a rule 25 resumption; rule 25 places a supplied subject or a second realization of one written phrase, not an object the Hebrew never wrote."
  ]
